# Technical Fixes for OutlookClient & Orchestrator

This plan addresses 4 critical issues identified in the Outlook integration:
1. **OData Date Filtering:** Ensuring date ranges are passed to the API to avoid excessive fetching and fixing client-side bypasses.
2. **Event Conflict Validation:** Adding overlap detection when creating calendar events.
3. **'Mark as Read' Implementation:** Adding a functional way to update the read status of emails.
4. **Mock Data Transparency:** Clearly identifying when the bot is returning mock data to avoid confusion.

## Proposed Changes

### [OutlookClient](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py)

#### [MODIFY] [outlook_client.py](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py)
- **[get_emails](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py#108-196)**: 
    - Re-introduce OData filters for `since_date` and `until_date` to reduce API payload, but keep client-side checks for timezone accuracy.
    - Updated mock data to include a `[DEMO]` prefix in subjects so the user (and AI) knows the data isn't live.
- **`mark_as_read(email_id)`**: [NEW] Add a method to perform a `PATCH` request to `/me/messages/{id}` to set `isRead: true`.
- **`check_calendar_overlap(start_str, end_str)`**: [NEW] Add a method to query events in the given time range and return a list of conflicts.
- **[create_event](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py#406-444)**: Update to call `check_calendar_overlap` first and return a warning if conflicts exist.

